think Round opened clean on f3d03055ba, twelve dead-letter entries reported, already on the anointed order.
think Read the card whole. The agent-doable queue's top item this lane could take -- %793's ordered-list spine -- was claimed by bakery fifteen minutes earlier at 20260916.220657, which the claim board answered before any edit. That is the coordination clause working in the direction it was widened for yesterday.
think Air's instruction is to press a claimed boundary and feel whether the hand passes through. Pressed three law-room boundaries and all three held: every one of 56 .claude/rules pages carries a .cursor twin on disk, every twin path a rule page claims resolves, and the baton's fourteen sections match the table in .claude/rules/the-baton.md one for one.
think The fourth gave. tools/fixtures/p/prose_register_scan.sh reads the law room at Gauge's Field target of 30 percent and eight pages stood over it, the worst at 55.
think Reached first for an excuse rather than a sweep: a rule page is a page about refusal, so Gauge's Meter clause -- uncapped, because refusal is the subject -- arguably reaches it. Ruling that by reading gauge-style.md alone would have been REDS %765 exactly: a law read correctly and still the wrong law.
obs So the excuse was measured instead of argued. Refusal words per 1,000 across all 56 law pages -- never, refuse, refusal, forbidden, forbids, bypass, banned, declines -- read 7.9 over the target and 7.0 under it. The same density. The room's densest page, .claude/rules/mind-source-adaptation.md at 26.8, sits UNDER target at zero percent: eight refusal words in 298, every one an active verb (Admit one, Refuse generated, Stop on ambiguity).
obs That refutes the excuse from the room's own bytes, and it names the technique the under-target pages already use: state a wall as an active verb rather than as a negated clause. The Field target is the right instrument for a law page.
obs The hot scoped endurance run found a red of my own, seven laps after it landed. reds_status_consistency reads verdict=ledger_contradicts_itself: %792, which I wrote last lap, quotes %730's closing line, and the scan decides a closure claim by word proximity to close/closes/closed/closing/closure. The noun phrase carries the word. Nothing in the ledger is actually inconsistent -- %730 is open and %792 says so. Booked at stamp 20260916.224600 with the repair specified rather than built: hold the proximity rule to verb forms, exclude closing followed by line, sentence, word or paragraph, and prove it from both sides on this real pair replayed from history.
obs The send's rebase met the derived spine's own founding case. I read --next from the anointed remote and got 794; a peer had booked 794 at 20260916.220113, half an hour before my 20260916.224600, and had pushed 795 beside it. The key is the stamp, so the earlier stamp keeps the number and my unshared row renumbered to %796 -- the law's rule 3 doing exactly its work, with no published byte moved. The recital conflict was the two folds meeting in one file and both lines belong.
obs Building that repair inside a send already carrying a sweep, a fold and a shelf is how a repair becomes its own red -- the sentence I wrote in %793 one lap ago. So it stands OPEN with its specification.
obs fold_shelf_link_repoint was red on two files: the shelf I wrote this lap, whose quoted elder link sat one directory too shallow, and a peer's shelf from 20260916.214125 carrying the same fault already. The tree's own repointer applied both. A guard that reds on a peer's file and on mine in one pass is the shared tree working as one tree.
obs Four other guards stand red and none is mine: rune_assert_sweep is named inside pheromone's live claim, built_tool_freshness wants the rye rebuild the card already names, and unheard_guard's refusal cascades into law_guard_heard, which reads its sibling's answer by design.
obs The counted sentences of .claude/rules/git-signing.md read the other way -- never bypass, no secret key on purpose, the hook refuses, there is no bypass -- and softening one would weaken the law. That page keeps its 55 percent honestly and stays on the printout.
